# Large media assets — too big for git, served from /var/www directly.
# If you reinstall the server from scratch, these need to be restored
# manually (look in backups, or re-export from local copies).
demo.mp4
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm

# install.sh + enroll.py are NOT canonical here. The source of truth
# lives in github.com/pensados/sentinelx-cloud-installer. They get
# copied into this directory at deploy time so nginx can serve them
# at https://get.sentinelx.app/install.sh.
#
# Tracking them here would mean two sources of truth that can drift.
# Always edit them in sentinelx-cloud-installer, then sync over.
install.sh
enroll.py

# Editor backups (sentinel_edit leaves these on failed transactions)
*.bak.*
*.bak

# OS clutter
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor scratch
*.swp
*~
